1
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,520
That mother and son

2
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,160
can't be trusted.

3
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:45,520
They steal phones,
then pretend to be good citizens.

4
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,480
I think it's best

5
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,800
we don't associate with them anymore.

6
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,720
Let her go!

7
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,400
Run!

8
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:57,880
Dad! He's been shot.

9
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:00,520
My head hurts so bad.
I can't take it anymore.

10
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,640
Uh, Mr. Nimit--

11
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,360
Walai, Rawee's been shot.

12
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,320
Please do what I suggested.

13
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:09,600
Tell Ms. Nada that Korn is her son.

14
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,520
Do you remember this ring?

15
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:15,360
Da, I think you should take a DNA test.

16
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,960
No. I won't take one.

17
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:23,040
Ms. Nada Tayawat is my mother.

18
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,880
Are you a rich kid, Wee?

19
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,240
We have to switch places, Korn.

20
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,480
Oh, it's you.

21
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,840
Looks like we meet again.
Do you remember me?

22
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,520
Yes, I do.

23
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,160
Are you from around here?

24
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:08,840
Yes, I am.

25
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,840
-You--
-Hold the elevator, please!

26
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:22,079
I still haven't forgotten
about your hair tie.

27
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,240
Korn.

28
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:06,000
This is Ms. Nada Tayawat.

29
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,600
Your biological mother.

30
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,000
-I…
-I…

31
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,320
You go first.

32
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,600
I want us to clear up
the misunderstanding.

33
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,840
So you and your aunt
will stop looking down on us.

34
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:08,200
I'm not a thief.

35
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:12,320
I was helping my friend
escape from a group of thugs.

36
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,360
I ran into you by accident,
and your phone fell.

37
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:21,280
I was going to return it.
I never meant to steal it.

38
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:26,160
I realize I was wrong about you.

39
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,840
I came here to thank you

40
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,800
and apologize.

41
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:42,320
You lost a great opportunity
because of me.

42
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:45,200
My family is willing
to help you continue your studies--

43
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,440
Forget it.

44
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:54,000
I'll find my own way through this.
I won't trouble you.

45
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,040
If my father were still alive,

46
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:02,120
he'd probably say

47
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,640
this was karma bringing us together,

48
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:09,320
so we could make things right.

49
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,560
And now, this is where it ends.

50
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:15,880
Yes.

51
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,960
I guess we won't see each other again.

52
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:23,000
My father is sending me
to study in America for my safety.

53
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,560
That's for the best.

54
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:30,280
I don't want to go.

55
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,280
If I were you, I'd go.

56
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,760
For your safety.

57
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,320
And to put your father's mind at ease.

58
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,400
The longer you stay here,

59
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,640
the more your father's enemies
will watch you.

60
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,760
To be honest,

61
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,120
you're his weak point.

62
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,680
So no one else
will get hurt because of me, right?

63
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:09,040
Sorry, that was an intrusive thought.

64
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,080
I believe

65
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:21,440
you'll recover and get back
to playing the football you love.

66
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,520
Thank you again for saving me.

67
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:31,360
I hope you get well soon.

68
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,799
I'll be going now.

69
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,360
I don't remember the name you gave him.

70
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,120
For his safety,

71
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:25,040
I gave him a new name, Phakorn.

72
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,480
Don't be afraid, my son.

73
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:41,600
I'll take you to Bangkok for treatment.

74
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,240
You'll get better soon.

75
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,880
I have to help you

76
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:50,000
make up for all the years
I wasn't there for you.

77
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:05,120
Mrs. Walai, I'll send Phakorn
to Bangkok today.

78
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:09,840
I'm just not ready yet.

79
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:14,720
Why not, my son?
Your condition could worsen at any time.

80
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:20,000
Well…

81
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:24,400
I want to spend one last time
with my family first.

82
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,120
Why would you say that?

83
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,960
This isn't the last time.

84
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:37,080
You'll be safe. You'll get better soon.

85
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:58,480
Alyssa, why didn't you tell me
where you were going?

86
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:01,720
I called you, but you didn't answer.
Do you know how worried I was?

87
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,840
I already sent you a message.

88
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,360
I only just saw it.

89
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,520
And why did you go visit him?

90
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:15,120
Aunt Pat, he saved my life.

91
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,560
If he hadn't followed me out,
I don't know where--

92
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:20,720
Alright. That's enough.

93
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,960
The important thing is that you're safe.

94
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:26,640
As for repaying that guy for saving you,

95
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:31,280
leave that to your father.
Don't get involved, okay?

96
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,280
Is Dad back yet?

97
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,920
Have you caught the person
who did this, Dad?

98
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:48,040
It was Uncle Jak's man, wasn't it?

99
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:51,400
I've taken care of everything.
Don't worry.

100
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,160
You're sending me away to study

101
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:58,400
for my safety, right?

102
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:01,840
If I leave, who will look after you?
Will you be safe?

103
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:05,160
Listen. He won't dare do anything to me.

104
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:08,240
Not as long
as he doesn't have the inheritance.

105
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:11,640
I've already taken care of the will.
He knows that.

106
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,480
It really was Uncle Jak.

107
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,600
I don't understand.

108
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,360
Why don't we just report him
and have him arrested?

109
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,360
Jak is my younger brother.

110
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:26,520
Your brother who tried to kill me?

111
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,960
He wasn't trying to kill you.

112
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:32,400
He only wanted to use you
to force me to change the will.

113
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,920
Someone like that is terrifying.

114
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,440
You shouldn't even keep him by your side.

115
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:42,600
I've sent him to Tawan Island.
I've had him watched. He can't leave

116
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,960
without my permission.

117
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:46,840
Trust me. He won't dare do anything.

118
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,960
If I agree to study abroad,

119
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:56,240
you have to promise me something.

120
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:59,480
Promise you'll take care
of your own safety too.

121
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:01,880
I promise.

122
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:06,240
But I want you to study hard for yourself

123
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,600
and come back
to carry on everything I've built.

124
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:12,960
-Can you do that?
-Of course.

125
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:17,640
I'll make Uncle Jak admit

126
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:22,280
that I'm the right person
to inherit your business.

127
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:26,040
Your decision is the right one.

128
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:29,080
You can trust me.

129
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:47,760
You didn't have to move in with me.
You were fine in your own room.

130
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,960
Someone was being dramatic, saying,

131
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:54,720
"I want to spend one last time
with my family."

132
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:58,440
Whoa, Mom snitched on me, didn't she?

133
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:02,800
She was going to send me to Bangkok today.
If I hadn't made a fuss,

134
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,520
would she have let me stay?

135
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,240
What about you, Wee?

136
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:08,880
If I wasn't around,

137
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:12,560
you'd miss me so much
you wouldn't be able to eat or sleep.

138
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,680
Wee.

139
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,640
After surgery,

140
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,920
is there a chance
I won't remember anything?

141
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:30,880
Anything can happen, Korn.

142
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,800
Don't worry about it too much.

143
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,840
How can I not worry?

144
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:40,520
What if I forget Mom and you?

145
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,200
She's a billionaire.

146
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:47,720
She'll find the best doctors to treat you.

147
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,720
Where's my phone?

148
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,480
It's right here.

149
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:11,960
What are you doing?

150
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:15,280
Well, I'm recording a video as proof.

151
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:19,720
If I forget everything,
just show me this video.

152
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:26,040
This is Wee, Rawee.
He's your older brother.

153
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,360
We grew up together.

154
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:31,680
He's both your friend and your brother.
He's someone

155
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,800
you love more than anyone.

156
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:39,040
If you're watching this video,
you have to remember him.

157
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:41,280
Don't ever forget him.

158
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:45,440
Because the man beside you
is the person who loves you the most.

159
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:49,320
He'll always help you,
support you in everything,

160
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:51,120
and you can trust him.

161
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:00,040
What's this? Are you about to cry?

162
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:02,680
Wow, you're such a crybaby.

163
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:06,440
Alright, that's enough.
You'll remember me.

164
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:10,160
One last question. A very important one.

165
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:11,800
You have to answer.

166
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,760
Do you love me?

167
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,000
I do.

168
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,520
I love you very much.

169
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:26,960
Happy now?

170
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:29,600
Heard that?

171
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:37,400
Keep it safe, okay?

172
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:53,560
I did the right thing, didn't I?

173
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:58,480
Sending our son away
to live with someone else.

174
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,760
I did the right thing, didn't I?

175
00:17:05,319 --> 00:17:08,720
Trying to save Phakorn's life.

176
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:14,280
<i>I have a favor to ask of you, Mrs. Walai.</i>

177
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,359
Of course.

178
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:22,000
I have to be honest with you.
I'm not my family's favorite.

179
00:17:22,079 --> 00:17:24,319
My relatives don't really like me either.

180
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,359
Since Phakorn is my son,

181
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:29,680
he'll naturally face opposition.

182
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:33,520
And as the first and only grandson
of the family,

183
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:36,360
they won't accept him easily.

184
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:40,160
That sounds really difficult.

185
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:43,840
I hope it won't be as serious
as what happened with Mr. Rawich.

186
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:48,680
No. Today is different from back then.

187
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,920
I'm the vice president
of Tayawat Group now.

188
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:56,120
Even if they don't like me,
they won't dare go against me.

189
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,680
Hearing you say that
makes me feel a little better.

190
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:03,080
So what can I do to help?

191
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:07,320
After I send Phakorn
to Bangkok for treatment,

192
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:11,760
I want you and your family
to stop contacting him for a while.

193
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,920
I need to take precautions first.

194
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,680
Otherwise, my family will keep digging

195
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:22,040
into Phakorn's background,

196
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:25,600
and it will end up affecting

197
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:27,520
you and your family too.

198
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,560
More importantly,

199
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:34,800
they'll interfere
with Phakorn's treatment,

200
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,880
and things won't go smoothly.

201
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:43,800
Once everything is settled,
I'll contact you again.

202
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,160
We need to help each other

203
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,640
for Phakorn's future.

204
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:18,200
-Slowly, Wee.
-Okay.

205
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,920
-Here.
-Hold on.

206
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,400
-Can you handle it?
-Careful, son.

207
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:24,680
-Let me help.
-Want a piggyback ride?

208
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,560
Do you think you can?

209
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:28,840
You're asking for trouble.

210
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,840
You're not exactly strong either.

211
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:32,560
Come on, Mom.

212
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:36,880
Let me take care of Wee for once.
He's so small. It'll be easy.

213
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,320
-You're something.
-Alright.

214
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,720
Steady now.

215
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,120
-Slowly.
-Yeah.

216
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,520
One, two.

217
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,680
Ms. Nada.

218
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,240
Put it on speaker, Mom.

219
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,040
Yes, Ms. Nada.

220
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,920
<i>His surgery is scheduled for next week.</i>

221
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:01,320
We're very lucky. Another patient
rescheduled their appointment.

222
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:04,760
I see.

223
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:07,280
When should I bring him in?

224
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,880
I'll come pick him up myself.

225
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:13,000
Let's make it Friday afternoon.

226
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,160
Okay.

227
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,920
Where are you, Pim?

228
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:32,080
Hey, I'm so happy for you.

229
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:35,720
You suddenly found your long-lost nephew.

230
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:40,400
Well, Nada already found the son

231
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,680
she left with someone else.

232
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:44,840
So apparently,

233
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:48,520
after seeing her own handwriting
in the diary

234
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,280
and the family ring,

235
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:53,400
she suddenly remembered everything.

236
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:56,960
I'm happy for you.

237
00:20:57,040 --> 00:21:00,880
Now you have a grown nephew
to share the inheritance with.

238
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,760
That's it for today's report.

239
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,000
Goodbye.

240
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:14,520
Alyssa, did you arrange to meet
the senior about your studies?

241
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:18,600
Yes. Uncle Chai
will take me there this Friday.

242
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:21,680
Okay. Do you want me to go with you?

243
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,440
I can reschedule my dentist appointment.

244
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:26,520
It's okay.

245
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:30,600
I thought we'd get lunch after.
I don't want them to feel awkward.

246
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,560
Okay, sure.

247
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:34,240
Yes.

248
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:41,080
Jang! Do you know yet?

249
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,680
PIMPA

250
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,840
What is it?

251
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:01,280
It took you forever to answer.

252
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,760
I wouldn't have called
if it wasn't important.

253
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,320
Just say it.

254
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:15,200
This is definitely the ring
our father had made.

255
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:20,400
Is this evidence really enough?

256
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:24,800
I remember everything now.
Isn't that enough?

257
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:27,320
What about a DNA test?
Why won't you do it?

258
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,600
I won't.

259
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:32,880
I already feel terrible enough
for what I did to my son.

260
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:42,920
All this time, you all knew I had a son.

261
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,720
So why did you all stay silent?

262
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,960
Ugh.

263
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:49,560
Everyone thought your son was dead.

264
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:51,080
Who would dare bring it up again?

265
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:54,800
And what if you lost control again
and forgot everything?

266
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,920
Father would have blamed me for it.

267
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:00,760
I was only trying to help.

268
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:02,440
Was it really to help,

269
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:06,400
or did you just not want
the family's first grandson

270
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:08,400
to be my son?

271
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,640
Then let's wait until Father
comes back from Germany.

272
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:13,720
Show him this evidence.

273
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,240
Let's see

274
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:19,040
if he'll accept this kid as his grandson.

275
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,480
Whether he accepts him or not,

276
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:24,960
I will never make my son take a DNA test.

277
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:30,040
It's just a DNA test.
It'll give us proof and make things clear.

278
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:32,520
Hey.

279
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:34,680
This is a respected family, you know.

280
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:37,360
Not your mother's common family,

281
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:40,440
where you can just bring anyone
into the family.

282
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,000
There's a lot of inheritance at stake.

283
00:23:47,840 --> 00:23:49,400
Worried about sharing the inheritance?

284
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:55,920
I'm comfortable with my decision.

285
00:23:57,120 --> 00:24:00,160
If I have to hurt my son
by making him take a DNA test

286
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:03,440
just to satisfy other people,
I won't do it.

287
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,360
That's all.

288
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:09,320
Wait, Da.

289
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:12,640
Why don't you bring him to meet Father?

290
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,840
Then we'll see who he looks like.

291
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:19,520
You or Rawich.

292
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:23,760
I'll bring him. But not now.

293
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:27,720
Why not? What's the big secret?

294
00:24:48,080 --> 00:24:50,480
Need anything from the bathroom, Korn?

295
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:52,000
No, I'm good.

296
00:24:56,520 --> 00:24:58,200
Anything else I can help with?

297
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:02,160
Just stay here and cheer me on.
That's enough.

298
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:11,560
Uh, Wee.

299
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,040
Yeah?

300
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:23,480
When I recover from the surgery,

301
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:26,280
you have to tell Ms. Nada the truth.

302
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:29,760
I've already decided.

303
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:32,200
I think I'd rather not tell her.

304
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:34,680
Why?

305
00:25:35,880 --> 00:25:39,360
You're smarter than me.
You're quicker-witted.

306
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:43,880
I think they'll accept you
more easily than me.

307
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:47,080
But your family is rich.

308
00:25:47,600 --> 00:25:49,560
Why give up
such a great opportunity for me?

309
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:52,160
I don't think
I'm losing an opportunity, Korn.

310
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,800
I think I'm creating
a better opportunity instead.

311
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:57,440
You'll get a higher education

312
00:25:58,040 --> 00:25:59,720
and a job at Tayawat Group.

313
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:05,320
Someone as slow as me
could never do as well as you.

314
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:14,080
Once you're settled,
you can come back and help us.

315
00:26:15,520 --> 00:26:16,800
I don't know why,

316
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:20,280
but it feels like
I'm taking advantage of you.

317
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:23,280
Don't think like that, Korn.

318
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:26,360
We're both making sacrifices.

319
00:26:27,280 --> 00:26:30,200
You have to leave your family
and live with strangers.

320
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:33,320
If you look at it that way,

321
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:37,520
I'd feel selfish too
for taking advantage of you.

322
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:43,120
Then I promise.

323
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:48,080
I'll bring our family back
to how it was when Dad was here.

324
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:56,600
I'll be here to see you succeed.

325
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:04,000
You crybaby.

326
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:39,480
Hello, Ms. Nada.

327
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:44,480
The house was hard to find, wasn't it?
Please come in.

328
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:01,040
I have an announcement to make.

329
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,440
After Phakorn recovers from surgery,

330
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:10,080
I'll send him to study in America.

331
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,320
Why so soon?

332
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:18,800
My family still doesn't accept him.

333
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:20,960
They'll probably interfere,

334
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:24,840
and this won't end easily.
So I'm dealing with it now.

335
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:34,880
But right now, I have a problem
with Phakorn's records.

336
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:40,840
Previously, there was a court order

337
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:43,920
declaring Phakorn missing.

338
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:48,320
It will take a long time
to gather the evidence

339
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:50,800
and confirm his true identity,

340
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:53,160
and I can't wait that long.

341
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:56,920
So I'll send Phakorn to study in America

342
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,280
as Mrs. Walai's son first.

343
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:03,800
Okay. Do whatever is convenient for you.

344
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:05,920
Thank you.

345
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:12,160
Mr. Thamrong will help coordinate
the documents and evidence with you.

346
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,360
Okay.

347
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:35,840
And please don't forget
what I asked of you.

348
00:29:38,040 --> 00:29:42,080
Stop contacting Phakorn
until everything is settled.

349
00:29:54,040 --> 00:29:55,840
Shall we go, Phakorn?

350
00:29:59,280 --> 00:30:00,240
Yes.

351
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:20,600
Hey, Korn.

352
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:23,640
Don't be afraid of the pain.

353
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:28,240
You won't feel anything.
Just sleep for a while, and it'll be over.

354
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:34,360
Will they shave my head?

355
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:37,440
I'm more worried
about not looking handsome.

356
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:44,880
How about this? Once the surgery is over,

357
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:47,640
call me right away, okay?

358
00:30:57,000 --> 00:31:00,720
Don't worry. I'll take care of Phakorn
until he recovers.

359
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:02,400
He will get better.

360
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:05,480
Thank you.

361
00:31:06,240 --> 00:31:08,520
I should thank you again, Mrs. Walai,

362
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:11,520
for taking such good care of Phakorn.

363
00:31:17,240 --> 00:31:18,760
Shall we go, Phakorn?

364
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:21,680
Yes.

365
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:34,760
May you be protected
and kept safe, my son.

366
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:37,600
May your surgery go smoothly

367
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:40,920
and you recover soon.

368
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:45,280
I love you, Mom.

369
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:56,320
Please take good care of yourself too.

370
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:08,200
No, it's okay.

371
00:33:11,040 --> 00:33:13,120
Aren't you going to say goodbye to them?

372
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:16,600
I don't want to look weak
in front of others.

373
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:20,320
It's better to look ahead.

374
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:42,280
It feels like she wants Korn
to cut ties with our family, Mom.

375
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:46,840
Ms. Nada has to do this
for your brother's safety.

376
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:49,000
Let's go inside.

377
00:33:51,640 --> 00:33:52,960
Do you need my help?

378
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:54,440
Thank you.

379
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:30,199
-Auntie.
-Thank you.

380
00:34:31,040 --> 00:34:33,800
I came to apologize again

381
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:36,800
for being the reason your son got hurt.

382
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:41,239
It's not your fault at all.
You didn't do anything wrong.

383
00:34:42,239 --> 00:34:45,480
Have the police caught the person
who did it yet?

384
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:46,679
Well…

385
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:50,800
I think Dad said he'd already handled it.

386
00:34:55,199 --> 00:34:57,640
Do you want to see him? I'll go get him.

387
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:01,440
He's still having trouble walking
and needs his cane.

388
00:35:01,520 --> 00:35:03,000
I'll go get him for you.

389
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:04,600
Oh, no, it's okay.

390
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:07,480
It's okay. Maybe it's better not to.

391
00:35:09,840 --> 00:35:11,080
Auntie.

392
00:35:11,600 --> 00:35:14,720
If there's anything I can do to help you,
please tell me.

393
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:18,240
I'd be more than happy to help.

394
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:24,800
My family doesn't hold
anything against you.

395
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:26,680
Hey.

396
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:31,760
You don't have to think about it so much.

397
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:36,920
Okay.

398
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:01,520
How did you find my house?

399
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:08,840
Actually, I shouldn't have asked.

400
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:11,600
It wouldn't be difficult
for someone like you.

401
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:18,640
I just want to say,
don't come to my house again.

402
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:23,000
Your aunt might get upset
and blame my mother and my family again.

403
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:28,520
We've apologized and thanked each other.
Let's leave it at that.

404
00:36:29,640 --> 00:36:33,200
Because if this hadn't happened,
someone like you

405
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:35,800
would never have wanted
anything to do with me.

406
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:39,040
Yes.

407
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:44,680
I won't come here again.

408
00:36:47,880 --> 00:36:49,080
I should get going.

409
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:29,040
Korn?

410
00:37:29,120 --> 00:37:30,720
Mom, it's Ms. Nada.

411
00:37:33,040 --> 00:37:36,520
Hello, Ms. Nada. How is Korn?
Did the surgery go well?

412
00:37:37,200 --> 00:37:40,320
Everything went well. Phakorn is safe now.

413
00:37:40,400 --> 00:37:41,320
Yes!

414
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:43,080
What a relief.

415
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:47,000
Ask her, Mom.
Ask if Korn remembers everything.

416
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:51,760
Does Korn remember everything clearly?

417
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:56,040
From what we've checked so far,
he remembers everything normally.

418
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,320
I see.

419
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,040
Mom!

420
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:04,000
He made it, Mom.

421
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,200
Mom.

422
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:11,720
Mom, can I go to Bangkok tomorrow
to see him?

423
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:14,920
But Ms. Nada asked us not to.

424
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:18,240
I can just go without telling her, right?
I need to see for myself

425
00:38:18,320 --> 00:38:20,160
that he's okay.

426
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:25,000
Please, Mom.

427
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:26,960
Please let me go.

428
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:30,600
Please, Mom.

429
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:47,560
You…

430
00:38:52,640 --> 00:38:54,600
You two already know each other?

431
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:59,440
We've just met before.
We don't know each other.

432
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:04,520
This is Phakorn, my son.

433
00:39:05,040 --> 00:39:08,600
And this is Alyssa,
the daughter of my friend, Mr. Nimit.

434
00:39:11,240 --> 00:39:12,360
Hello.

435
00:39:17,240 --> 00:39:18,200
Are you feeling better?

436
00:39:19,960 --> 00:39:21,280
Much better now.

437
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:22,320
Good.

438
00:39:23,520 --> 00:39:25,920
So when did you two meet?

439
00:39:27,040 --> 00:39:29,720
A while ago. At the library.

440
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:33,320
I didn't expect
the world to be this small.

441
00:39:35,120 --> 00:39:36,720
This actually makes things easier.

442
00:39:37,240 --> 00:39:41,480
I talked to Mr. Nimit
about sending you to study in America.

443
00:39:42,200 --> 00:39:44,360
And Alyssa is going there too.

444
00:39:45,200 --> 00:39:47,760
Since you'll be in the same place,
you can look out for each other.

445
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:52,600
That's great.
Then they can fly there together.

446
00:39:52,680 --> 00:39:53,840
Right?

447
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:59,440
How are the documents coming along?

448
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:03,200
Everything is ready.
We just need the medical certificate.

449
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:07,960
If I'd known we'd meet again,
I would've brought your hat back.

450
00:40:10,160 --> 00:40:13,240
But I brought your hair tie.

451
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:22,000
After this, I think
we'll be seeing each other a lot more.

452
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:23,680
Can I keep it for now?

453
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:27,960
Is this a hostage?

454
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:30,280
Yes.

455
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:39,760
When we met last time,
I didn't know you were seriously ill.

456
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,440
I'm sorry I didn't ask.

457
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,120
It's okay.

458
00:40:44,840 --> 00:40:47,160
By the way,
who were you visiting back then?

459
00:40:54,120 --> 00:40:55,200
Hello?

460
00:40:56,600 --> 00:40:57,640
What?

461
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:05,920
Excuse me for a moment.
I have something to take care of.

462
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Of course. Then I'll take my leave.

463
00:41:09,600 --> 00:41:10,440
Alright.

464
00:41:11,200 --> 00:41:12,320
Alyssa.

465
00:41:13,200 --> 00:41:16,160
Let's go. Phakorn needs to rest too.

466
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:18,160
-Okay.
-Get well soon.

467
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,480
Thank you.

468
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:23,160
Goodbye, Auntie.

469
00:41:24,200 --> 00:41:25,240
Let's go.

470
00:41:37,040 --> 00:41:40,560
PHAKORN TAYAWAT

471
00:41:58,840 --> 00:41:59,800
Korn.

472
00:42:01,640 --> 00:42:02,680
PHAKORN TAYAWAT

473
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:06,800
Pim!

474
00:42:10,600 --> 00:42:12,240
Isn't this going too far?

475
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:15,880
I told you already,
I'm not ready for you to meet my son.

476
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:19,000
Why? I'm his aunt.

477
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:21,240
What's wrong
with wanting to see my nephew?

478
00:42:22,040 --> 00:42:23,200
Move aside.

479
00:42:35,400 --> 00:42:36,320
You were quick.

480
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:40,000
I think your source got something wrong.

481
00:42:41,480 --> 00:42:44,360
I think there's something suspicious
going on here.

482
00:42:44,960 --> 00:42:47,720
You found your son,
but won't bring him to meet the family?

483
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:50,440
Because I'm afraid my son

484
00:42:50,520 --> 00:42:52,400
will meet the same fate as his father.

485
00:42:53,600 --> 00:42:56,560
Are you accusing me
of hiring someone to kill your husband?

486
00:42:56,640 --> 00:42:59,240
We still don't know who killed him.

487
00:42:59,320 --> 00:43:00,840
Everyone is a suspect.

488
00:43:03,840 --> 00:43:05,640
Keep avoiding me if you can.

489
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:07,680
Pim.

490
00:43:07,760 --> 00:43:10,200
If you don't stop harassing my son,

491
00:43:10,280 --> 00:43:13,920
I'll have your position changed again.

492
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,320
Are you threatening me again?

493
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,320
It's not a threat.

494
00:43:17,080 --> 00:43:19,200
There are some executives

495
00:43:19,280 --> 00:43:20,640
who aren't performing well.

496
00:43:20,720 --> 00:43:22,720
If she weren't his daughter,

497
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:24,400
no one would keep her around.

498
00:43:27,280 --> 00:43:28,720
Hey, Nada!

499
00:43:28,800 --> 00:43:29,680
Who are you talking about?

500
00:43:29,760 --> 00:43:30,600
Who do you mean?

501
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:50,120
This is one of the perks of being rich.

502
00:45:00,600 --> 00:45:02,280
Oh, Alyssa.

503
00:45:02,360 --> 00:45:04,400
Dad told me you arrived today.

504
00:45:05,440 --> 00:45:08,000
I was just thinking about you. Come in.

505
00:45:15,240 --> 00:45:18,480
The room is nice.
It's close to the university too.

506
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:21,640
Thank you for taking care of everything.

507
00:45:22,760 --> 00:45:24,480
Is your place far from here?

508
00:45:25,520 --> 00:45:28,000
Not far. Just two blocks away.

509
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:31,760
Do you want to see the university?
I'll take you there.

510
00:45:32,880 --> 00:45:33,720
Sure.

511
00:45:42,160 --> 00:45:43,400
What's all this?

512
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:47,000
I went to Thai Town.
I was craving basil stir-fry so badly.

513
00:45:47,880 --> 00:45:50,320
I'll show you my cooking skills
and make basil stir-fry for you.

514
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:59,400
A rich kid like you
can cook basil stir-fry?

515
00:45:59,920 --> 00:46:01,760
Wait till you taste
this rich kid's cooking.

516
00:46:39,360 --> 00:46:40,440
She's intense.

517
00:46:41,640 --> 00:46:43,320
Kick you out first.

518
00:46:43,960 --> 00:46:46,080
I told you not to put in so much basil.

519
00:46:46,160 --> 00:46:48,000
But you wanted to eat it, didn't you?

520
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:50,760
I almost died.

521
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:54,800
-Hey! Turn it off.
-Turn it off.

522
00:47:04,360 --> 00:47:06,080
Happy birthday.

523
00:47:13,600 --> 00:47:16,640
I made this cake especially for you.

524
00:47:18,680 --> 00:47:19,840
It's beautiful.

525
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:21,760
And it tastes good too.

526
00:49:00,840 --> 00:49:02,120
Alyssa.

527
00:49:02,840 --> 00:49:04,320
Alyssa.

528
00:49:05,440 --> 00:49:09,920
I'm sorry, Alyssa.
I didn't mean to rush you.

529
00:49:13,360 --> 00:49:15,920
But I want you to know

530
00:49:16,520 --> 00:49:18,160
that I'm serious.

531
00:49:19,080 --> 00:49:21,400
And I really like you.

532
00:49:31,120 --> 00:49:32,680
Will you be my girlfriend?

533
00:49:45,360 --> 00:49:48,040
It's not that I don't feel good about you.

534
00:49:48,920 --> 00:49:51,680
Things are really good here
because I have you with me.

535
00:49:53,840 --> 00:49:56,840
But what I mean is, right now,

536
00:49:57,680 --> 00:49:59,840
I'm not thinking about this.

537
00:50:02,520 --> 00:50:03,760
Then…

538
00:50:05,400 --> 00:50:07,400
Can you give me a chance?

539
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:09,960
Give us a chance
to get to know each other.

540
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:13,120
And I promise I won't rush you.

541
00:50:22,120 --> 00:50:25,080
I don't want to become
someone who's selfish.

542
00:50:26,640 --> 00:50:30,800
Let's say, if I start feeling
the same way about you,

543
00:50:32,640 --> 00:50:34,320
we can try dating.

544
00:50:35,680 --> 00:50:39,280
If you don't want to wait,
that's okay too.

545
00:50:41,320 --> 00:50:43,040
No, Alyssa.

546
00:50:43,120 --> 00:50:44,640
I'm not going anywhere.

547
00:50:45,680 --> 00:50:47,360
Please give me a chance.

548
00:50:58,640 --> 00:51:02,200
THREE YEARS LATER

549
00:51:18,160 --> 00:51:19,600
Wee, you should go now.

550
00:51:21,720 --> 00:51:22,760
Yes, Mom.

551
00:51:39,760 --> 00:51:41,720
Alright.

552
00:51:41,800 --> 00:51:43,120
Let's go.

553
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:47,480
Put it here.

554
00:51:50,040 --> 00:51:51,560
I'll go get the others first.

555
00:51:51,640 --> 00:51:54,000
Mom, I'll come help during my lunch break.

556
00:51:54,080 --> 00:51:54,880
Okay, dear.

557
00:52:10,240 --> 00:52:11,400
Come in.

558
00:52:14,480 --> 00:52:16,320
Here are all the flight details.

559
00:52:16,400 --> 00:52:17,320
Thank you very much.

560
00:52:18,520 --> 00:52:19,400
Uncle.

561
00:52:19,960 --> 00:52:21,600
Is Ms. Alyssa coming back?

562
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:25,280
Yes. She has to come back
to help her father with the business.

563
00:52:26,680 --> 00:52:28,440
By the way, how is Phakorn doing?

564
00:52:29,360 --> 00:52:31,000
I haven't heard from him at all.

565
00:52:31,520 --> 00:52:35,600
Ms. Nada told us not to contact him,
so I haven't reached out.

566
00:52:37,840 --> 00:52:39,800
I think that's for the best.

567
00:52:41,280 --> 00:52:42,680
Ms. Nada's life

568
00:52:44,040 --> 00:52:47,200
isn't as easy as it may seem to you.

569
00:52:48,320 --> 00:52:52,000
She's always had to prove herself
to her father and siblings.

570
00:52:55,280 --> 00:52:56,280
Rawee.

571
00:52:57,600 --> 00:52:59,640
Honestly, Ms. Nada has been through a lot.

572
00:53:01,360 --> 00:53:04,880
She's always seemed
to be on her own and lonely.

573
00:53:04,960 --> 00:53:07,760
But luckily, she found her son.

574
00:53:09,800 --> 00:53:12,960
So don't be angry or upset with her.

575
00:53:14,120 --> 00:53:15,680
Everything she did

576
00:53:15,760 --> 00:53:17,720
was only to protect herself.

577
00:53:21,520 --> 00:53:22,680
Yes, Uncle.

578
00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:28,840
Thank you. I'll let you know
once I have Alyssa's return date.

579
00:53:28,920 --> 00:53:30,080
Yes.

580
00:53:35,480 --> 00:53:36,560
Wee!

581
00:53:36,640 --> 00:53:37,480
Yes?

582
00:53:37,560 --> 00:53:40,840
Hurry, go check on your mother.
She's having chest pain again.

583
00:53:48,000 --> 00:53:49,240
Thank you.

584
00:53:54,360 --> 00:53:56,440
You all got too worried.

585
00:53:56,520 --> 00:53:59,720
I told you I just needed some rest.
The medicine helped.

586
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:04,240
You didn't need to bring me here.
I feel bad troubling Mr. Nimit.

587
00:54:05,800 --> 00:54:07,800
It was good that we got you checked, Mom.

588
00:54:08,400 --> 00:54:09,520
So we can rest easy.

589
00:54:18,880 --> 00:54:21,920
-Ms. Nada. Hello.
-Hello.

590
00:54:25,040 --> 00:54:26,840
Hello, Ms. Nada.

591
00:54:27,440 --> 00:54:28,880
-How are you feeling?
-Much better.

592
00:54:28,960 --> 00:54:31,320
How did you know Mom was sick?

593
00:54:32,160 --> 00:54:36,320
I was on my way to see Mr. Nimit,
so I stopped by when I heard.

594
00:54:36,840 --> 00:54:39,120
And I came to share
some good news with everyone.

595
00:54:41,840 --> 00:54:44,880
Phakorn has graduated.
He's coming back to Thailand.

596
00:54:45,760 --> 00:54:46,800
Really?

597
00:54:46,880 --> 00:54:48,040
Yes.

598
00:54:48,120 --> 00:54:51,480
At first, he didn't want to come back.
He wanted to continue studying.

599
00:54:51,560 --> 00:54:56,440
But I told him we needed his help
with a big project, and he agreed.

600
00:54:57,040 --> 00:54:59,280
Can we finally see Korn?

601
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:02,680
Of course. My family

602
00:55:02,760 --> 00:55:04,560
has finally accepted Phakorn.

603
00:55:05,080 --> 00:55:06,800
He's such a talented student.

604
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:15,440
I also came to ask you
to come work at the company.

605
00:55:17,120 --> 00:55:18,120
Really?

606
00:55:20,240 --> 00:55:23,720
Wee, thank Ms. Nada.

607
00:55:27,840 --> 00:55:30,760
I really want you
to come work for the company.

608
00:55:31,520 --> 00:55:32,640
I'm not forcing you.

609
00:55:33,240 --> 00:55:35,560
The decision is yours.

610
00:55:37,160 --> 00:55:39,360
But I'd be disappointed if you said no.

611
00:55:59,200 --> 00:56:00,160
What is it, Mom?

612
00:56:02,040 --> 00:56:04,560
Have you called Ms. Nada's secretary yet?

613
00:56:05,720 --> 00:56:06,960
Not yet.

614
00:56:07,800 --> 00:56:10,640
Oh my, it's been almost a week already.

615
00:56:10,720 --> 00:56:13,880
You should give them a clear answer
either way.

616
00:56:13,960 --> 00:56:15,720
It's the polite thing to do.

617
00:56:20,400 --> 00:56:22,760
I just haven't made up my mind yet.

618
00:56:30,680 --> 00:56:33,200
Then let me decide for you.

619
00:56:38,040 --> 00:56:40,400
I want you to work with Ms. Nada.

620
00:56:42,160 --> 00:56:45,040
It'll be a chance for you
to work at a big company.

621
00:56:47,640 --> 00:56:48,800
And…

622
00:56:51,640 --> 00:56:54,040
You'll get to be closer
to your real mother.

623
00:56:55,960 --> 00:56:58,720
That's exactly why I don't want to go.

624
00:57:08,440 --> 00:57:11,520
But it would help me
feel less guilty, Wee.

625
00:57:15,560 --> 00:57:18,400
I want you to have
good opportunities in life.

626
00:57:20,560 --> 00:57:23,480
When Korn comes back,
you'll have each other.

627
00:57:24,440 --> 00:57:27,800
The two of you can help each other,
and I won't have to worry anymore.

628
00:57:32,320 --> 00:57:33,400
Please, son.

629
00:58:11,720 --> 00:58:14,920
Hello. I'm Taddao, Ms. Nada's secretary.

630
00:58:15,520 --> 00:58:18,320
-This way, Mr. Phakorn.
-Yes.

631
00:58:37,520 --> 00:58:39,800
This is your office, Mr. Phakorn.

632
00:58:40,320 --> 00:58:42,320
You'll be responsible for brand strategy

633
00:58:42,960 --> 00:58:45,480
as the Vice President of Brand Strategy.

634
00:58:46,320 --> 00:58:49,520
If you need anything, press ten

635
00:58:49,600 --> 00:58:51,240
to reach me.

636
00:59:23,800 --> 00:59:24,680
Come in.

637
00:59:33,560 --> 00:59:34,920
Korn.

638
00:59:41,720 --> 00:59:42,840
Whose car is that?

639
00:59:46,920 --> 00:59:48,520
<i>Have you told anyone the truth, Wee?</i>

640
00:59:48,600 --> 00:59:50,320
<i>About the two of us switching places.</i>

641
00:59:50,400 --> 00:59:53,320
<i>If they don't accept us,</i>
<i>we can just stay like this, Korn.</i>

642
00:59:53,400 --> 00:59:56,440
<i>I've come too far, Wee.</i>
<i>I don't want to go back.</i>

643
00:59:56,520 --> 00:59:58,360
Don't tell me you still don't know.

644
00:59:58,960 --> 01:00:01,960
Your mother was the daughter
of a mistress.

645
01:00:03,640 --> 01:00:06,520
<i>Don't let anyone look down on us, Korn.</i>

646
01:00:06,600 --> 01:00:09,480
If we show weakness,
we'll lose everything.

647
01:00:09,560 --> 01:00:12,000
You have to defeat everyone

648
01:00:12,600 --> 01:00:14,080
with your own ability, like I did.

649
01:00:24,760 --> 01:00:27,080
<i>I didn't think</i>
<i>the world would be this small.</i>

650
01:00:27,680 --> 01:00:29,640
Looks like we'll be seeing
each other more often.

651
01:01:08,280 --> 01:01:10,000
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
